<title>UK: European cotton demand slows.</title>
<headline>European cotton demand slows.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Demand remains subdued in many European cotton markets as the summer holidays make an impact, traders said.</p>
<p>Small sales of Central Asian styles are understood to have been made to the Czech Republic and Spanish new crop descriptions have attracted attention in Portugal.</p>
<p>Other business has included additional sales of U.S. cottons to Turkey, for nearby shipment.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
